lls are crucial for you to  navigate in the working environment to  form peer to peer comradery  maybe that is why companies spend lots  of money training employers for work  ethics and personality development  according to linkedin's research 89  percent of talent acquisition managers  believe that when a new hire doesn't  work out it's because they lack critical  soft skills moreover this survey also  highlights that 57 percent of employers  value soft skills over hard skills when  it comes to hiring new candidates some  examples of soft skills are  communication  empathy  adaptability  critical thinking  teamwork and responsibility  you can hone these skills by yourself  learning and practice here's a video to  help you figure out how you can ace  these valuable skills moving ahead we  will discover how we can accentuate hard  skills in soft skills  first we will look at the ways to  highlight hard skins  your resume is the most appropriate  place to exhibit your technical  expertise hence we suggest you to go  through the job descriptions before  formatting your resume  compare your skill set to the skills  needed for the job and add the skills  that are there to both lists  for example if you are aspiring to  become a software developer then  highlighting command over programming  languages like java python or c plus  along with proper certifications will  give you instant credibility you can  also add details of your internship  certifications and projects to your  resume  recruiters prefer students who have  internship experiences as they seem more  thorough with practical knowledge  during the interviews you can highlight  the projects and real-life incidents  where you solve the problems on your own  use more quantitative examples rather  than vague examples to show your skills  effectively  now let's understand the ways to  highlight soft skills soft skills are  personality traits that are evaluated in  interview rounds  the first move you can make to show